From 5305827f80630f27cebadc1a553ae98b9c434d7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:23:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 steps 2 and 3: Orekit and Basilisk adapters and notebooks
 read back the trajectory Kshana writes, with a difference report and a CI
 workflow

integrations/flight-dynamics/: kshana_fd.py (writes the OEM, OPM and SPK through the
Python binding, checks the pinned SHA-256 and, with KSHANA_FD_CLI_DIR, the command line's
bytes; reads back what was written; the difference report), orekit_reader.py (Orekit's
OemParser and OpmParser through orekit_jpype 13.1.9.0, orekit-data at a pinned commit),
basilisk_reader.py (Basilisk 2.12.2's own SPICE, pyswice: dafgda_c records and spkezr_c
at the nodes), the two notebooks (.md mirror and .ipynb) and run_notebooks.py.

Results on the CAPSTONE table: Orekit carries the OEM (4,321 states) and the OPM: every
value is Orekit's km-to-m conversion of the written double, every epoch the written one;
the report names Orekit as rounding further than the digits written (that conversion is a
second rounding, at most 1 ulp; worst 2.83 half-units of the last digit). Basilisk reads
the SPK's 25,926 stored values and 4,321 epochs with the written bits; spkezr_c at the
nodes within 1.5e-11 km.

.github/workflows/flight-dynamics.yml: one job builds the command line, runs
`kshana connect check`, writes the files and builds the wheel; a matrix job runs each
tool's notebook top to bottom and uploads its report. web/smoke.mjs checks that the
WebAssembly ephem_export gives the pinned bytes.
